&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;About StarRez&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;StarRez is the global leader in student housing software, providing innovative solutions for on and off-campus housing management, resident wellness and experience, and revenue generation. Trusted by 1,400+ clients across 25+ countries, StarRez supports more than 4 million beds annually with its user-friendly, all-in-one platform, delivering seamless experiences for students and administrators. With offices in the United States, Australia, the UK, and India, StarRez blends the robust capabilities of a global organization with the personalized care and service of a trusted partner.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #0075db; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #0075db; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have an uncanny knack for problem solving and you have a sharp product mindset. Our Tech Leads are involved in all aspects of the software design process and create high-performing, scalable, and secure products. This is a hands-on technical role, with no people management responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the most senior technical person in your team, you’ll be hands-on in the solution and code, working alongside Product, Design, Quality, Platform, Security and your team to design solutions that power a new market-leading Analytics platform. You aren’t afraid to challenge the status quo and define solutions that sit outside of existing patterns, especially where reliability, security, and repeatability are critical to customer success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will own the engineering foundations of StarRez’s Analytics &amp;amp; Reporting capabilities, leading the development of a new Analytics product and the implementation of a new cloud data warehouse. You will lead the build of the data model integration layer, including automated customer schema provisioning, user provisioning, and Single Sign-On (SSO) integration (SAML/OIDC) to deliver a seamless and secure customer experience. You will also uplift existing ad-hoc reporting and analytics tools, and assist with improving the StarRez database schema, working closely with Data Analysts, Engineers and Product Managers to align the platform to best practice and analytics readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Inter, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;With deep knowledge of your domain and programming language, you not only understand how choices made in software design and architecture affect areas like performance, maintainability, testability, observability, and security, you teach and promote this knowledge to others within and across teams. You are hands-on and keep up to date with the latest .NET and web technologies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #0075db; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #0075db; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have held a Technical Lead (or similar role) for at least 2 years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have worked to improve, modernise and decompose large codebases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience creating products and features from the ground up, and successfully taking them through to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on SaaS platforms at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing and building integration-heavy systems (APIs, automation, workflows) with a focus on reliability and security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing identity and access patterns, including SSO (SAML/OIDC), role/group mapping, and least-privilege access models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong database fundamentals and practical SQL experience; comfortable designing safe schema changes and performance-minded data access patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An inclination towards communication, inclusion, and visibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of .NET ecosystem (framework 4.6+ / .NET 6+)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Web technologies – C#, MVC, HTML, JavaScript, CSS etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with testing frameworks in C#&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Azure SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Git&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #0075db; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #0075db; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of CI/CD pipelines and DevOps principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with one or more public cloud providers such as Azure, AWS or GCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building foundations for modern analytics/data platforms and cloud data warehouses (e.g., Snowflake, Azure Synapse, Microsoft Fabric)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data pipeline tooling and patterns (e.g., Azure Data Factory, Snowflake Openflow, Fivetran, dbt, or similar tools)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with multi-tenant SaaS analytics patterns (tenant isolation, RBAC, auditability, and data access controls such as row-level security where applicable)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational mindset: observability/monitoring, runbooks, incident response, and production support readiness for GA launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accessibility &amp;amp; accessible UI development (WCAG/ARIA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
